            {
                "entry_id": "e476d23a-786c-3c48-9b1b-33b80b7e8ded",
                "word": "néper",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e3c3d591-ccc7-4022-8914-635558710336",
                        "entry_id": "e476d23a-786c-3c48-9b1b-33b80b7e8ded",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "népers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "daeee8a8-c4fe-3ad9-87b7-ac675651c539",
                        "entry_id": "e476d23a-786c-3c48-9b1b-33b80b7e8ded",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unité sans dimension, de symbole Np, utilisée avec le Système international (SI) mais n’en faisant pas partie, servant à exprimer les rapports de grandeurs de même espèce. Le néper est le logarithme naturel de ce rapport : autrement dit, un rapport de e:1 vaut 1 Np (où e est le nombre d’Euler)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1620860d-6026-4f84-9c6d-6d6e3f45ffa0",
                                "sense_id": "daeee8a8-c4fe-3ad9-87b7-ac675651c539",
                                "text": "L'amortissement ou affaiblissement se mesure par comparaison entre la puissance émise et la puissance reçue, et se chiffre en népers. Un néper exprime que le rapport des deux grandeurs comparées est égale à la base des logarithmes naturels e = 2,718. La relation donnant le nombre de népers N est donc : N=logna/b."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e66fad00-7ef1-4b0b-84ed-9e880484b8ab",
                                "sense_id": "daeee8a8-c4fe-3ad9-87b7-ac675651c539",
                                "text": "Un néper correspond à un rapport e de deux grandeurs de champ. On vérifie que 1 dB = 0,115 Np et 1 Np = 8,69 dB."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a41b06a-4422-4dcf-a8f7-a49d9e3fe103",
                        "source_entry_id": "e476d23a-786c-3c48-9b1b-33b80b7e8ded",
                        "source_sense_id": "daeee8a8-c4fe-3ad9-87b7-ac675651c539",
                        "target_lang_word": "Neper",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0771eec-47e0-4adf-9941-d379708930f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "e476d23a-786c-3c48-9b1b-33b80b7e8ded",
                        "source_sense_id": "daeee8a8-c4fe-3ad9-87b7-ac675651c539",
                        "target_lang_word": "neper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "neper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11c2a137-90f7-3585-b24f-1feecf467661",
                                        "entry_id": "b46978c8-cb46-35ce-bb00-eaa9444162fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-SI unit of the attenuation (or sometimes gain) of field and power quantities such as electronic signals; the natural logarithm of a ratio, with 1 Np (a ratio of 2.718:1) being equivalent to 8.686 dB."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65b4349e-36b8-467a-be6a-662b7b6ba150",
                                                "sense_id": "11c2a137-90f7-3585-b24f-1feecf467661",
                                                "text": "Values of b, the amplitude attenuation constant, are given for various materials in Table 1.1. Having dimensions of [length]⁻¹, it is usually measured in nepers per centimetre (Np cm⁻¹)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fc148a5-7fac-4020-b9be-d4a6fd21ef5c",
                                                "sense_id": "11c2a137-90f7-3585-b24f-1feecf467661",
                                                "text": "The unit of α is nepers per meter. It can be easily seen that if a line has an attenuation constant of 1 neper/m, a unit amplitude voltage wave will reduce to e⁻¹ over a distance of 1 meter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd19031d-8fb7-4787-a856-27e7504a42d0",
                                                "sense_id": "11c2a137-90f7-3585-b24f-1feecf467661",
                                                "text": "The attenuation constant for the phantom muscle tissue is αₘ = 10.0 nepers/m."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
